error[SC0009]: `q` is not a valid numeric literal suffix
  --> tests/ui/several_errors_in_one_file.science:16:22
   |
16 |     let counted be 42q
   |                      ^ unknown suffix
   |
   = note: the suffixes are `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `i64`, `u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `f32` and `f64`

error[SC0010]: `2` is not a valid digit in a binary literal
  --> tests/ui/several_errors_in_one_file.science:17:22
   |
17 |     let mask be 0b1012
   |                      ^ invalid digit

error[SC0003]: tabs are not allowed in indentation
  --> tests/ui/several_errors_in_one_file.science:18:1
   |
18 | 	let indented_with_a_tab be 0
   | ^ tab character in the indentation
   |
   = note: Science does not interpret tabs: their width depends on how the file is displayed, so a block would mean different things to different readers. Indent with spaces only.
